; Lead: BrokkAi/bifrost-packs#443 (requests CVE-2026-25645).
; os.path.join(tempfile.gettempdir(), NAME) with a fixed NAME is a path every
; local user can predict. On a shared /tmp another user can create that file or
; a symlink first, so code that reuses an existing file at that path trusts
; content someone else wrote, and code that writes there can be redirected.
; requests < 2.33.0 wrote its CA bundle to such a path and reused it when it
; existed, so a local user chose which certificates requests trusted.
;
; Engine contract: the subject is an exact call to tempfile.gettempdir (typeshed
; identity) that is the first of exactly two arguments to a call spelled join,
; whose second argument is a string literal. A literal that interpolates a call,
; such as f"{uuid.uuid4()}.pem", is excluded, because the call may supply a
; random part. The join call is matched by its spelling, because os.path.join
; and posixpath.join do not bind to an exact identity on Bifrost 0.15.4.
;
; This belongs in insecure-temporary-file (same CWE and remediation). It is a
; separate rule for now because that rule's tempfile.mktemp locator resolves to
; two exact identities on Bifrost 0.15.4 with packs/v0.16.0 (the typeshed pack
; and bifrost.python-stdlib-api-declarations both declare it), which leaves the
; whole rule not_run. Merge the two once that ambiguity is resolved.
(policy
  :schema-version 1
  :id "bifrost.security.python.predictable-temporary-path"
  :name "Python predictable path in the shared temporary directory"
  :message "A fixed file name is joined onto tempfile.gettempdir(), so other local users can predict and pre-create the path"
  :severity warning
  :description "Reports os.path.join(tempfile.gettempdir(), NAME) where NAME is a string literal. The temporary directory is usually shared, so another local user can create the file or a symlink at that path first; code that reuses or writes the file then trusts or overwrites content it does not control (CWE-377, requests CVE-2026-25645). Subject identity is the exact tempfile.gettempdir call."
  :help-uri "https://bifrost.brokk.ai/static-analysis-policies/#built-in-security-pack"
  :tags ["security" "python" "filesystem" "temporary-file" "cwe-377"]
  :analysis (analysis
    :type assertion
    (bind :name predictable-temporary-path :query
      (rql :schema-version 1
        (resolved-call :resolves-to "tempfile.gettempdir" :proof exact
          (call-bindings (call-shape (language python
            (inside
              (call :callee (name "join") (arity 2)
                :args [(call :callee (name "gettempdir")) (string_literal :not-has (call))])
              (call :callee (name "gettempdir")))))))))
    (group :name by-call :by (predictable-temporary-path.site_id)
      (aggregate :name predictable-paths :op count))
    (assert :group by-call :value predictable-paths :cardinality (exactly 0)))
  :classification (classification
    :fallback (classification-id :taxonomy "CWE" :id "377")))
